"use strict";(self.webpackChunk_N_E=self.webpackChunk_N_E||[]).push([[3999],{3999:function(n){n.exports=JSON.parse('{"content":"\\n## Efficient Node.js Management using NVM (Node Version Manager)\\nUsing <mark>NVM (Node Version Manager)</mark> makes it easy to switch between different Node.js versions for each project, making development environment configuration much more pleasant.\\n### Install NVM\\nExecute the NVM installation script by entering the command below in the terminal.  \\nYou can check for the latest version and modify it as needed before installation.\\n```sh\\n{\\n    \\"title\\": \\"Install NVM\\"\\n}\\n---\\ncurl -o- https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nvm-sh/nvm/v0.39.7/install.sh | bash\\n# Or using wget\\nwget -qO- https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nvm-sh/nvm/v0.39.7/install.sh | bash\\n```\\n### Configure Shell\\nAfter installation, the settings are added to your shell environment file (such as `~/.zshrc` or `~/.bashrc`).  \\nTo apply the changes immediately, enter the following command.\\n```sh\\n{\\n    \\"title\\": \\"Apply configure in shell\\"\\n}\\n---\\n$ source ~/.zshrc  # Zsh\\n# or\\n$ source ~/.bash_profile # Bash\\n```\\n### Install Node.js\\nIf <mark>NVM</mark> is installed correctly, you can now install the desired version of Node.js.  \\nI recommend installing the `latest LTS` version.\\n```sh\\n{\\n    \\"title\\": \\"Install Node.js\\"\\n}\\n---\\n$ nvm install --lts\\n```\\nSpecific versions can also be installed.\\n```sh\\n{\\n    \\"title\\": \\"Install specific version of Node.js\\"\\n}\\n---\\n$ nvm install 18.17.0\\n```\\n### Manage Versions\\nYou can check installed versions or switch between them freely.\\n| Command | Description |\\n| :--- | :--- |\\n| `nvm ls` | Check all installed Node versions |\\n| `nvm use <version>` | Switch to a specific version |\\n| `nvm alias default <version>` | Set default version when terminal starts |\\n"}')}}]);